# PHP & Home Assistant Add-on Container Guardrails

- All Lovelace operations (`lovelace/*`) are WebSocket-only via `sweethome3d/www/lib/LovelaceWs.php` (`ws://supervisor/core/websocket`). Never add REST calls to `supervisor/core/api/lovelace/*` or shell out to Python.
- Keep `clear_env = no` in `rootfs/etc/php82/php-fpm.conf` so `SUPERVISOR_TOKEN` stays visible to PHP-FPM workers.
- Preserve Nginx Brotli headers (`Content-Encoding: br`, `gzip off`) for `/unity-visualizer/*.br` assets and `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`.
- Keep LF (`\n`) line endings on all shell/s6 scripts under `rootfs/etc/cont-init.d/` and `rootfs/etc/services.d/`.
- Read `docs/ai/lovelace-ws.md` and `docs/ai/known-gotchas.md` before modifying HA integration endpoints.
